================================================================================
SCOPE OF THIS LICENSE, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER
================================================================================

The MIT grant above covers the work authored for this project:

  Geography/src/geography/**       the agent-based model (Java)
  scripts/**                       data acquisition, analysis, scenario
                                   construction, figure generation, validation
  docs/**                          documentation written for this project,
                                   EXCEPT the third-party items listed below
  Geography/batch/**               run configuration files
  Geography/data/registry/**       the variable and assumption registries
  Geography/data/shelters/*.csv    the shelter inventory compiled for this
                                   project from the public sources named in
                                   Geography/data/README.md

It does NOT cover the following, each of which carries its own terms. Nothing
here grants you any right to any of them.


1. REPAST SIMPHONY AND ITS DEPENDENCIES
   Geography/repast-licenses/     (41 dependency license texts)
   Geography/license.txt          (inherited statement from the stock demo)
   Geography/data/Agents2.*, CookCounty.*, WaterLines.*, Zones2.*,
   RGBTestPattern.*, SP27GTIF.TIF, UTM2GTIF.TIF, README.TXT
                                  (stock Repast Simphony demo data; retained
                                  because it is part of the inherited upstream
                                  project, and loaded by no code path here)

   Repast Simphony is distributed under its own terms; see
   Geography/repast-licenses/repast-license.txt. GeographicLib, the JTS
   Topology Suite and GeoTools likewise carry their own licenses, included in
   that directory.


2. THE SPRINGER CHAPTER CLASS
   docs/chapter/svmult.cls
   rubrik/OFFICIAL-template/**

   Copyright Springer-Verlag. Redistributed here only as supplied with the
   2026 Summer Proceedings chapter template, for the purpose of compiling this
   chapter. Not relicensed.


3. THE STREET CENTERLINE DATA  --  REDISTRIBUTION TERMS UNVERIFIED
   Geography/data/Streets.shp, .dbf, .shx, .prj, .cpg
   Streets.zip

   Portland Metro Regional Land Information System (RLIS) street centerlines,
   inferred from the attribute schema. This file was supplied with the
   inherited project and predates version control here: its original download
   date, RLIS release version, and redistribution license could NOT be
   recovered. This is documented as a known provenance gap in
   Geography/data/README.md and docs/science/DATA_SOURCES.md (source D0), and
   is stated in the published chapter.

   Treat its redistribution as unconfirmed. If you need this layer, obtain it
   directly from Metro / gis-pdx.opendata.arcgis.com under their terms rather
   than relying on the copy here.


4. PUBLIC-SECTOR DATA (redistributed, not owned)
   Geography/data/airnow/aqs_hourly_pm25_portland_2020-09.csv
       U.S. Environmental Protection Agency, Air Quality System. A work of the
       U.S. federal government and therefore in the public domain. EPA asks
       that AQS be acknowledged as the source.

   Geography/data/encampments/irp_campsite_reports_sample.csv
       City of Portland open data (Impact Reduction Program campsite reports).
       Subject to the City of Portland's open-data terms.

   Both are reproducible from their original sources by the fetch scripts in
   scripts/, and every file carries a SHA-256 checksum in
   Geography/data/README.md.


5. THIRD-PARTY DOCUMENTS INCLUDED FOR REFERENCE
   rubrik/EXAMPLE-chapter-VanPelt-2026.pdf
       Copyright Darcy Van Pelt. Included only as a worked example of the
       proceedings format.
   "Copy of Wildfires smoke.pdf"
       Project presentation slides; not relicensed.
   files (1)/wildfire-reu-package/**/source-pdfs/**
       Published reports retained for provenance verification. Each remains
       under its publisher's terms.


================================================================================
HOW TO CITE
================================================================================

If you use this model or its results, please cite the software (see
CITATION.cff) rather than only this license file. Results in the published
chapter were produced from a clean working tree; each run manifest records its
git commit, random seed, and a SHA-256 checksum for every input file, so any
reported number can be traced to the exact bytes that produced it.
